cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper and the two datasets
  listed under `references`. The datasets are not redistributed here.
title: "Two origins of feature redundancy: analysis code for qEEG and transcranial Doppler"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a matched-taxonomy comparison of feature redundancy in
  stroke-related quantitative EEG and transcranial Doppler ultrasound. Both
  descriptor sets are mapped onto one family taxonomy and reduced to an
  11-descriptor core identical in family structure and cardinality, then
  passed through one label-agnostic pipeline with every data-dependent step
  re-fitted inside each subject-grouped training fold. Redundancy is treated
  as the measured quantity rather than a nuisance, which separates algebraic
  redundancy (closed-form construction, dominant in TCD) from physiological
  redundancy (shared causes, dominant in qEEG).
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
keywords:
  - feature redundancy
  - quantitative EEG
  - transcranial Doppler
  - feature selection
  - equivalence testing
  - stroke
